  "description": "The 2026 election for Oklahoma's 5th Congressional District features incumbent Republican Rep. Stephanie Bice seeking a fourth term against a field that includes two independent candidates and the winner of the June 16 Democratic primary between Jena Nelson and Trey Martin. The district, which covers central Oklahoma including most of Oklahoma City and surrounding communities, was significantly redrawn after the 2020 census to include more rural areas. Bice has been rated as the strong favorite by nonpartisan election forecasters, though Democrats see a potential path following Kendra Horn's surprise 2018 win in the district's previous configuration. Key issues in the race include health care costs, education funding, immigration enforcement, and economic affordability.",
